/-!
# Cyclicity instances: `D = I_k` at dims 3-4, `𝕋 = ℤ[T₂]` at dim 2

Generated by `tools/gen_hecke_cyclic.py` (byte-identical re-runs; do not
hand-edit).  For each of the 18 level-one weights with `2 ≤ dim S_k ≤ 4`
(the dims 2-4 slice of the 54 verified Maeda weights):

* dims 3-4: `HeckeCyclicWeightKK.D_eq_Ik` — the reduced denominator `D` of
  the landed T₃ witness (`HeckeIndexWeightKK.Dn`, witness
  `HeckeRatWeightKK.cert`) equals the Hecke index `HeckeIndexWeightKK.Ik`.
  Route: the quotient `𝕋 ⧸ ℤ[T₂]` is generated by `[T₃]` (`T₁ = 1`,
  `T₄ = T₂² − 2^{k−1}T₁`), `D • T₃ ∈ ℤ[T₂]` (the landed certificate), so
  `I_k ∣ D`; with the landed `D ∣ I_k` and positivity, `D = I_k`.  The
  index cardinality enters as an explicit hypothesis `hcard : Nat.card
  (𝕋 ⧸ ℤ[T₂]) = Ik.natAbs` — b1's `HeckeLatticeIndex` index-card facts
  plug in here (blueprint index-card §0(iii)); until then the theorem is
  stated in this hypothesis form.  Also `heckeLattice_ne_t2Span`:
  `𝕋 ≠ ℤ[T₂]` at these weights (`I_k ≠ 1`, via the iff).
* dim 2: `heckeLattice_eq_t2Span` — `𝕋 = ℤ[T₂]` unconditionally: both
  lattices are `span ℤ {1, T₂}` (`heckeTM_id`), no index, no Maeda
  hypothesis (upgrades the F1 numerics `I_k = D = 1` to a lattice
  equality).

Everything is light: no `set_option`, no kernel decides except the
per-weight positivity/`≠ 1` checks (`norm_num` over literals).
-/

open HeckeIndex HeckeTM HeckeFieldRat MaedaLevelOne Polynomial
open UpperHalfPlane ModularForm CuspForm
